---
import Layout from "../../components/Layout.astro";
import DocShell from "../../components/DocShell.astro";
import CommandBlock from "../../components/CommandBlock.astro";
---

<Layout title="Fixture Harness | ArkheionX Docs" description="The deterministic local/static fixture benchmark harness in ArkheionX v3.9.0.">
  <DocShell>
    <p class="page-kicker">Model</p>
    <h1>Fixture harness.</h1>
    <p class="doc-deck">A controlled benchmark layer for checking ArkheionX artifact stability against nine small protocol shapes.</p>

    <h2>What is included</h2>
    <p>Three fixture sets contain nine static Solidity-like source inputs:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Set 1: token, lending vault, and staking/reward shapes.</li>
      <li>Set 2: AMM/swap, oracle-dependent vault, and upgradeable proxy shapes.</li>
      <li>Set 3: bridge/message, liquidation/borrow-repay, and governance/timelock shapes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What the benchmark checks</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Deterministic fixture, artifact, run, result, and suite IDs.</li>
      <li>Stable JSON-safe serialization.</li>
      <li>Path confinement to registered local fixture sources.</li>
      <li>Source SHA-256 fingerprints and byte sizes.</li>
      <li>Snapshot drift and safety-boundary flags.</li>
      <li>Copy scans that prevent unsupported claims from entering fixture output.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Python surface</h2>
    <CommandBlock
      title="python"
      command={`python3 - <<'PY'
import arkheionx.fixture_harness as fh

suite = fh.build_all_fixture_suite()
print(len(suite.fixtures))
print(suite.id)
PY`}
    />

    <h2>Boundary</h2>
    <p>
      The harness does not compile or execute fixture source. It does not perform network access. A passing fixture
      benchmark means the expected review infrastructure behavior remained stable for that controlled input; it says
      nothing final about the security of a real protocol.
    </p>
  </DocShell>
</Layout>
